\ ff-test: lines
\ Stack limits hold on every push, and hitting one leaves the engine usable.
\
\ The evaluator pushed literals with no overflow check: one push past the
\ top overwrote the stack's own bookkeeping. `execute` and deferred words
\ re-enter the interpreter, pushing a return frame nothing checked, so deep
\ recursion through them ran off the end of the return stack. And under
\ FF_R_TRUSTED, NEST / DO lost their overflow checks altogether, although
\ how deep a program recurses is up to the program.

: fill 512 0 do 0 loop ;
fill 1
clear fill 1.5
clear fill "s"
clear depth . cr

: r1 ['] r1 execute ;
r1
defer rd
: r2 rd ;
' r2 is rd
r2
: r3 1 r3 drop ;
r3
: r4 10 0 do r4 loop ;
r4
clear 1 2 + . cr
